# The Kali archive, for building the `security` variant.
#
# This file is not read by a desktop build: build/build.sh stages it into
# config/archives/ only when SAMURAI_VARIANT=security, and removes it otherwise,
# because live-build installs every config/archives/*.list.chroot it finds and
# has no notion of a variant.
#
# It is a `.chroot` file, so live-build writes it into the build chroot for the
# package-install pass and takes it out again afterwards; the copy meant for the
# image a user boots is kali.list.binary. Both are checked into the repository
# side by side rather than generated, so reading this directory says exactly
# which archives a given image was built against.
#
# https and not http: Debian's own mirror stays on http because it is
# authenticated by Release-file signature against the packaged Debian keyring,
# and the same is true here - but a third-party archive that can be replaced by
# anyone on the network path should not be given the benefit of the doubt.
#
# All four components exist in kali-rolling (verified against
# dists/kali-rolling/<component>/binary-amd64/Packages.gz before this file was
# written); a component that disappeared would fail `apt-get update` in the
# build rather than silently ship a shorter toolset.
deb [ arch=amd64 ] https://archive.kali.org/kali kali-rolling main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
